<div class="wrap"><div class="prose about-page">
  <p>Red Thread Labs LLC is my business helping people <em>practice</em> what is being preached. We hold labs and events that help people build long-lasting, authentic relationship skills.</p>
  <p>In our <strong>Practice Labs</strong> we use methods and teach skills that help people build new habits. The loops you acquired in childhood tend to run your love life, your friendships and your work. <strong>Change them once, and they change everywhere.</strong> We find the patterns, try out new skills, and actually shift behavior using evidence-based methods.</p>

  <h2>Practice Labs</h2>
  <p>Hands-on workshops for people who keep looping the same pattern and want to change it, whether you're dating, partnered for decades, or somewhere in between. You come as <em>the scientist of your own life</em>: you practice, notice what happens, and take the skill home.</p>

  <h2 id="coaching">Coaching</h2>
  <p>One-on-one, my work is grounded in transpersonal education and my Practice Labs methodology. Instead of talking around a problem, you learn how your mind builds the patterns you're stuck in, and how to rebuild them. <strong>Often a single two-hour block is enough to resolve many issues</strong>, and the tools stay with you long after.</p>
  <p><strong>Transpersonal education</strong> is learning that treats the whole person as the classroom: body, mind, emotions and spirit, including the experiences that don't fit neatly into a personal story. Its aim is growth and self-knowledge, not diagnosis or cure. It teaches you how your inner experience works so you can work with it yourself.</p>
  <p>I offer one-on-one and group sessions built around how you actually think and feel, with follow-ups and support between sessions. Book a free conversation to see if we have a fit.</p>

  <h2>Consultations</h2>
  <p>Teams and leadership, ceremonies and rituals, readings and spiritual consults, and <a href="/fashion/#styling">fashion and styling</a>, for when you need a focused session rather than an ongoing practice.</p>

